<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inti Raymi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Festival of the Sun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inti">Inti</a> Raymi, the Festival of the Sun, was the main religious festival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> at the June solstice in honour of the sun god Inti. Banned by the Spanish authorities in the 16th century, it was revived as a public spectacle in 1944 and is now staged each June at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacsayhuaman">Sacsayhuamán</a> above Cusco.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inti-raymi.jpg" alt="Inti Raymi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cyntia Motta · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inti_Raymi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
